# Line endings -- Windows / Git Bash support (claude-code/docs/15 section 10).
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which checks text files out with CRLF.
# bash then fails on every script ("$'\r': command not found", "set: pipefail\r: invalid
# option"), and Dockerfiles / gradlew / files mounted into Linux containers misbehave too.
# These attributes override core.autocrlf: every text file is checked out with LF on every
# platform. The index already stores LF, so nothing needs renormalizing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files keep the CRLF they are stored with.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text

# Binaries: never convert.
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.parquet binary
